BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Chair Yoga with Breann
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260525T090000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260525T100000
UID:200d086ef8737e9bc936443a6b4f2789@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Chair Yoga – Mondays at 9 AM Join us every Monday morning at
  9:00 AM for a gentle and accessible Chair Yoga class\, led by Breann\, a 
 certified trauma-sensitive yoga teacher and experienced massage therapist.
  Breann brings over 20 years of experience in guiding others toward greate
 r body awareness\, healing\, and relaxation. This class is designed for ev
 eryone – whether you are new to yoga\, have limited mobility\, or are lo
 oking for a mindful and soothing way to start your week. Chair Yoga allows
  you to experience the benefits of yoga without needing to get down on a m
 at. What to Expect: • Seated and standing postures using the chair for s
 upport • Gentle stretches to enhance flexibility • Breathing exercises
  to calm the mind and body • Movements to promote better circulation and
  balance ✨ No experience necessary – come as you are! Where: Wellness 
 Collective When: Every Monday at 9:00 AM Cost: By donation Let this practi
 ce be a moment of self-care and grounding in your week.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Tai Chi with Drew
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260525T171500
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260525T181500
UID:77ec7b954ddc99817c7a2d1c733b1854@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Among all forms of physical activity\, Tai Chi Ch’uan is per
 haps the most accessible\, convenient\, and economical way to improve both
  physical health and mental well-being. As Yang Style Tai Chi master Cheng
  Man-Ching once said\, ‘Those who understand the importance of exercise 
 for health will find Tai Chi Ch’uan indispensable.’ While Tai Chi may 
 not be easy to master\, consistent practice will yield results. In this cl
 ass\, we will focus on cultivating chi\, building endurance and strength\,
  and developing core alignment\, all while learning to release tension. Ta
 i Chi training offers many levels of progression. In Yang Style\, when pra
 cticed correctly\, it becomes an aerobic workout\, despite minimal movemen
 t. Additionally\, it serves as a form of meditation. Please wear comfortab
 le clothing. Flat shoes\, socks\, or bare feet are ideal. Students are enc
 ouraged to train at their own pace\, and progression will vary from person
  to person.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Intro to Mind series with Dana
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T070000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T074500
UID:2d6a2aa25f57264e3890a5c0777849e8@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Intro to Mind (ITM): A 9-Week Meditation Series with Dana This
  nine-week mind science series invites you to slow down\, notice\, and ste
 ady your mind — especially in the face of uncertainty. Together\, we’l
 l explore meditation in a practical\, approachable way. Each week explores
  simple tools you can use in daily life — when sitting\, moving\, and co
 nnecting with others. Over nine weeks\, we’ll also explore how water\, f
 ood\, sleep\, music\, movement\, stillness\, community\, and meditation sh
 ape how we live and how we experience the world — in a supportive commun
 ity of fellow practitioners. The series is divided into three parts: Weeks
  1–3: Mind at Rest During these weeks\, we’ll focus on finding moments
  of rest and steadiness in the space between thoughts and in the face of s
 ensations and emotions — especially when life feels busy or uncertain.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Chair Yoga @ the Grand Center-Bre
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T143000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T153000
UID:6b9e8a4fe6d9303942468e1bccf19165@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every Tuesday afternoon at 2:30 PM at the Grand Center
  for a gentle\, accessible Chair Yoga class led by rotating Wellness Colle
 ctive yoga instructors. Each teacher brings their own style and expertise\
 , while sharing a common focus on safety\, choice\, and ease in the body. 
 This class is especially supportive for older adults and anyone who prefer
 s to stay off the floor\, has limited mobility\, uses a chair for stabilit
 y\, or is simply looking for a calm\, nourishing way to move. All poses ar
 e done seated or standing with the support of a chair\, so you can experie
 nce the benefits of yoga without getting down on a mat.
LOCATION:Grand Center\, 182 N 500 W\, Moab\, UT 84532\, USA
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Relaxing Yoga and Meditation with Amanda
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T171500
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T181500
UID:7d3610dec03fa80527a4e1c338915925@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a slow\, supportive yoga practice designed to help the
  body and mind settle. Classes blend gentle movement\, yin and restorative
  postures\, and mindful transitions that prioritize comfort\, choice\, and
  ease. Each class includes a 10-minute meditation practice. You are always
  invited — never required — to participate in any way that feels right
  for you This class is open to all bodies and experience levels\, accessib
 le and adaptable\, and focused on relaxation\, presence\, and nervous syst
 em balance. Come as you are. Rest is welcome here.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Wellness Collective Moab": "https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wellness_collective
URL:https://wellnesscollectivemoab.com/calendar
SUMMARY:Acupuncture with Rob
DTSTART;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=MDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T193000
UID:0d5e29a21f3b3f65c89c2c7c750a9dd7@wellnesscollectivemoab.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the healing benefits of acupuncture in a supportive
 \, community setting. Led by Rob\, a licensed acupuncturist and naturopath
 ic physician\, this group offering is designed to promote relaxation\, bal
 ance the nervous system\, and support whole-person wellness. During each s
 ession\, participants will receive gentle acupuncture while resting comfor
 tably in a reclined position. Treatments are tailored to common concerns s
 uch as stress\, anxiety\, fatigue\, sleep disturbances\, and emotional ove
 rwhelm. No prior experience is needed\, and Rob will walk you through the 
 process so you feel at ease. Group acupuncture makes this powerful healing
  modality more accessible and affordable—while also allowing for shared 
 healing energy in community.
LOCATION:Wellness Collective\, 76 S 100 W\, Moab\, UT 84532
X-SOURCE:Wellness Collective Moab
END:VEVENT
